# core/data/talk/grammar/en/cool_blame.tlk - more replies to COMPLAIN and BLAME (owner: TK; T5b
# package T5B-COOL). Grumbling is a hobby in HELLvile: sympathy, shared moaning and sulky
# denial, clean in any room. No register word. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

# ---- COMPLAIN -> SYMPATHIZE / COMFORT ------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.complain.c_sympathize act: sympathize
  "Oh, that's awful. You poor thing. Do you want to sit down?"
  "Ugh, I'm so sorry. That sounds exhausting. And annoying."
  "That's rough, buddy. If it helps, I'm on your side."
  "Hang in there. It has to get better soon. Probably."
  "Aww, that's the worst. Come here, I'll moan with you."
  "I hear you. It's like the whole day got up wrong."
  "That would drive me round the bend. And I'm already round it."
  "You're allowed to be cross. I'd be furious. In a hat."
  "Terrible. Just terrible. Tell me more, I've got time."
  "Honestly? You deserve better. Better days, better snacks."
@rule core.complain.c_sympathize_polite guard: polite act: sympathize
  "Oh, how dreadful for you. Do sit down, I'll find some tea."
  "That does sound vexing. I'm so sorry you've had to bear it."
@rule core.complain.c_sympathize_elder guard: elder act: sympathize
  "There, there, dear. Life's a bumpy road. Mind the potholes."
  "I've had days like that, and weeks, and one whole decade."
@rule core.complain.c_sympathize_flat guard: flat act: sympathize
  "That's awful. {.}I'm feeling bad for you. It's the eyebrows."
  "Oh no, {.}Sorry. I'm sad on your behalf. Quietly."
@rule core.complain.c_sympathize_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: sympathize
  "Aw, that's no fun! Do you want half my biscuit?"
  "That's so sad! I'll be your friend until it's better!"
@rule core.complain.c_sympathize_x guard: topic act: sympathize
  "Ugh, {x}. Don't get me started. Actually, do, I'm ready."
  "{x:cap} again? The worst. The absolute worst, I tell you."
@rule core.complain.c_comfort act: comfort
  "Hey, it's okay. Take a breath. It'll pass, like a cloud."
  "Deep breath, in, out, see? Still here. Still excellent."
  "Listen, nothing lasts. Not even the bad stuff. That's the deal."
  "Tomorrow's a new day. A bit of a mess, but new."
  "You've survived every bad day so far. That's a hundred percent."
  "Let it out. I'll hold your sulk. It's light as a feather."
@rule core.complain.c_comfort_sad guard: mood=sad act: comfort
  "I'm not feeling great either. But we can be sad together."
  "Yeah, it's hard. I'll sit with you. Quietly, no jokes."

# ---- COMPLAIN -> AGREE / DISAGREE / COMPLAIN -----------------------------------------------------
@rule core.complain.c_agree act: agree
  "Right? It's outrageous. Someone should write a letter."
  "Yes! Exactly! I've been saying that since I got up."
  "Totally, it's a crime. I'm calling the Mayor. He'll nap."
  "Don't I know it. I've got a list. It's on the fridge."
  "You said it. I'd say it louder, but my voice is tired."
  "I'm with you all the way. Down the hill and back up."
  "That's what I told the cat! She just blinked. Rude."
  "Oh, absolutely. It's a scandal. I'm clutching my pearls."
@rule core.complain.c_agree_loud guard: loud act: agree
  "YES! IT'S OUTRAGEOUS! SOMEONE FETCH A MEGAPHONE!"
  "RIGHT?! I'VE BEEN SHOUTING IT FOR WEEKS! NOBODY LISTENS!"
@rule core.complain.c_agree_angry guard: mood=angry act: agree
  "Don't get me started! Actually, do. I've got a speech."
  "It makes my blood boil! And my tea, and my soup!"
@rule core.complain.c_agree_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: agree
  "I know! It's so not fair! Not fair at all!"
  "Yeah, totally! Grown-ups never listen! Except you."
@rule core.complain.c_disagree act: disagree
  "Oh, come on. It's not that bad. You're just hungry."
  "Hmm, I don't know. I think it's a bit nice, actually."
  "Eh, it's fine. Everything's fine. Fine is my brand."
  "You're being dramatic. I'm the dramatic one, back off."
  "I disagree. But I'll still listen. I love a good moan."
  "Really? I thought it was great. Maybe I'm just easy."
  "Nope. Not buying it. I've seen worse on a Wednesday."
@rule core.complain.c_disagree_blunt guard: blunt&!kid_present act: disagree
  "Stop whining. It's fine. Go eat something."
  "Meh. You're making it worse than it is. It's a Tuesday."
@rule core.complain.c_complain act: complain
  "You think that's bad? Wait till you hear mine. It's a saga."
  "Oh, don't start me. I've got three complaints, and a stool."
  "Same! Mine's worse though. Mine involves a duck."
  "Everything's wrong! Everything! Look at it all, wrong!"
  "Ugh, welcome to my life. It's a lot of this."
  "Don't, I've had a day. I've had two. They were both bad."
@rule core.complain.c_complain_flat guard: flat act: complain
  "Mm. {.}Also, I'm sad about it. This is my sad voice."
  "Tell me about it. {.}Or don't. I'll still be grumpy."
@rule core.complain.c_complain_quirky guard: quirky act: complain
  "It's the moon's fault. The moon's been rude all week."
  "I'm also upset! At a chair! It looked at me funny!"
@rule core.complain.c_dismiss tags: gentle act: dismiss
  "Boo hoo. Have a biscuit and sort it out." guard: !kid_present
  "That's life. Put a hat on it and keep walking."
  "Stop moaning, you big baby. And pass the salt." guard: !kid_present
  "Hm, and? Everyone's got problems. Mine's longer." guard: !kid_present
  "Wow, what a story. I'd feel for you, but I'm busy." guard: !kid_present
@rule core.complain.c_dismiss_polite guard: polite&!kid_present act: dismiss
  "I'm sure it will all come right in the end, dear. Do excuse me."
  "How trying. Well, I must be getting on. Lovely chat."
@rule core.complain.c_joke act: joke
  "Complaints? I've got a few. Would you like a number?"
  "I could moan about it too, but I'd have to book a room."
  "You should write that down. In a strongly worded cake."
  "Life's rough. Good thing we've got snacks and spite."
  "Don't fret, we'll all be ghosts someday. Think of the savings."
  "Ah, the sweet song of whining. It's my favourite lullaby."
@rule core.complain.c_tease guard: !kid_present act: tease
  "Aww, is somebody grumpy? Is it the big bad Thursday?"
  "Look at you, being all moany. It's adorable. Do a little more."
  "There it is. The famous grumble. Right on schedule."
  "Someone's grumpy. Don't let it hit the floor."

# ---- BLAME -> DISAGREE ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.blame.c_disagree act: disagree
  "Me? Never, I'm a model citizen. Ask the pigeons."
  "That's a lie, and a rude one. And I was nowhere near it."
  "Excuse me? I was reading. In another town, entirely."
  "I didn't do it. I was busy being innocent. It's exhausting."
  "How dare you. I've got an alibi. And a really nice hat."
  "It wasn't me! It was the guy with the hair. Nobody knows him."
  "I'm shocked. Shocked and appalled. And a little bit hungry."
  "You've got the wrong person. I'm much too lazy for that."
  "Nope, it was a goose. It's the geese. It's always the geese."
  "I want a lawyer. Specifically one with a cape."
@rule core.blame.c_disagree_loud guard: loud act: disagree
  "NOT ME, I WAS HERE! EVERYONE SAW ME! I WAS VERY LOUD!"
  "THAT'S A LIE! I DEMAND A RECOUNT! AND A SANDWICH!"
@rule core.blame.c_disagree_polite guard: polite act: disagree
  "I'm afraid there's been a misunderstanding. I was not involved."
  "Oh, I do beg your pardon, but you've mistaken me for someone guilty."
@rule core.blame.c_disagree_flat guard: flat act: disagree
  "No, {.}It wasn't me. This is my innocent face, see? Flat."
  "I didn't. {.}I'd tell you. I'm too tired to lie."
@rule core.blame.c_disagree_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: disagree
  "It wasn't me! It was the dog! We don't have a dog!"
  "Nuh-uh, I didn't do it! I promise! Cross my heart!"
@rule core.blame.c_disagree_elder guard: elder act: disagree
  "I'd never, dear. I've been in my chair since Tuesday."
  "Pish! I was asleep. It's the only thing I do on time."
@rule core.blame.c_disagree_x guard: topic act: disagree
  "It was {x:s} fault, not mine! Go and blame {x}!"
  "Don't look at me! Blame {x}! It's always {x}!"

# ---- BLAME -> APOLOGIZE / BLAME / COMPLAIN / DISMISS / JOKE -----------------------------------------
@rule core.blame.c_apologize act: apologize
  "Okay, okay, it was me. I'm sorry. I'll clean it up."
  "Ugh, fine. Guilty, I did it. I regret it a bit."
  "That was my fault. I'm sorry. I'll make it up to you."
  "I knew I'd get caught. I always do. It's my face."
  "You're right. I'm the culprit. Please be gentle with the verdict."
  "Sorry! I panicked! Next time I'll do it quieter."
@rule core.blame.c_apologize_polite guard: polite act: apologize
  "I owe you an apology, and a pie. Both are on their way."
  "How embarrassing. Yes, that was me. I'm truly sorry."
@rule core.blame.c_apologize_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: apologize
  "I'm sorry, it was me! Don't be mad! I'll tidy!"
  "Okay, it was me, I was scared, sorry. Can I have a hug? Or not."
@rule core.blame.c_blame tags: gentle act: blame
  "Excuse me? That was YOU! You held the ladder!" guard: !kid_present
  "Oh, so it's my fault? Who left the door open? Hm?" guard: !kid_present
  "No way. If anyone's to blame, it's you. And the weather." guard: !kid_present
  "Don't pin it on me. I've got a very slippery back."
  "You started it! You're always starting it! It's your hobby!" guard: !kid_present
  "Blame me? Fine, then I'm blaming you. Back to square one." guard: !kid_present
@rule core.blame.c_blame_blunt guard: blunt&!kid_present act: blame
  "Stop passing the buck. It's yours. You broke it, you bought it."
  "Look in a mirror. That's the culprit. Gorgeous, but guilty."
@rule core.blame.c_blame_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: blame
  "It was YOU! You did it first! I only did the second part!"
  "No, you! You, you, you! I'm telling!"
@rule core.blame.c_complain act: complain
  "Why does everyone always blame me? I'm a delight!"
  "That's so unfair. I'm the nicest person here. By far."
  "Well, that's lovely. Being accused before lunch. Thank you."
  "It's always me, isn't it? Never the vase. The vase is a menace."
  "Ugh, great. Another thing I didn't do. My list is long."
@rule core.blame.c_dismiss tags: gentle act: dismiss
  "Think what you like. I've got a clear conscience and a nap."
  "Blame away. The rain doesn't mind. It's used to it."
  "Meh. Take it up with someone who cares. It's a short list." guard: !kid_present
  "Sure, sure. Put it on my tab. I've got an infinite tab."
@rule core.blame.c_joke act: joke
  "Fine, it was me. And the butler. And a sneaky cat."
  "I'm always the prime suspect. It's an honour. I want a badge."
  "Whodunit? Me done it, well, a bit. In a suit, with a candle."
  "You'll never prove it. I've covered my tracks. With glitter."
  "Guilty! Of being fabulous. The rest is hearsay."
